# f32.convert_i64_s and f32.convert_i64_u round once, to the nearest f32 with
# ties to even, for every input: 2^24+1, 2^53+1, inputs one past an f32
# half-way point (2^62+2^38+1 and 0x8000_0080_0000_0001, where rounding
# through f64 first lands on the tie and rounds down), u64 max and i64 min,
# on the default and release tiers. f64.convert_i64_u also rounds once above
# 2^53, a tie included, and never stops.
